$$
F_{\text{grav}} = F_{\text{electro}}
$$

Using Newton’s law of gravitation and Coulomb’s law:

$$
\frac{G M_{\text{earth}} M_{\text{moon}}}{r^2} = \frac{k Q^2}{r^2}
$$

The $ r^2 $ terms cancel out, leaving:

$$
G M_{\text{earth}} M_{\text{moon}} = k Q^2
$$

Solving for $ Q $:

$$
Q = \sqrt{ \frac{G M_{\text{earth}} M_{\text{moon}}}{k} }
